    <h1>Sources</h1>
    <p>Primary notes we actually used. Retailer blogs are not listed unless they were the only public trail for a brand.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>AR Blue Clean, “Get Connected | Understanding M22 Hose fittings” (2 June 2026) — stem vs thread, 14-into-15 leak behavior, adapters. <a href="https://arblueclean.com/blog/get-connected-understanding-m22-hose-fittings/">arblueclean.com</a></li>
      <li>Shop Joe / Sun Joe, high-pressure hose compatibility and third-party accessory FAQs — M22-15 mm on many unit outlets; M22 14 mm / 15 mm accessory language. <a href="https://support.shopjoe.com/">support.shopjoe.com</a></li>
      <li>Kärcher K-series aftermarket adapters sold as clip × M22-14 mm (multiple EU/AU retailers) — confirms the consumer K clip is not M22.</li>
      <li>ASME B1.20.7 — garden hose thread (GHT / NH), commonly 3/4-11.5. Summarized on engineering references; we do not reproduce the standard.</li>
      <li>ASME B1.20.1 — NPT. Cited only to keep GHT and NPT apart.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If a page says “commonly reported,” it means aftermarket listings agreed and no OEM chart was on the first results page. Send a manual excerpt via <a href="/contact/">contact</a> and we will upgrade the confidence label.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
